Levels: Gates

Purpose:
  Defines gate levels L0-L5 and default gate matrix.

Levels:
  L0:
    Description: Prototype
    Checks: Minimal
  L1:
    Description: Small project
    Checks: Basic test + lint
  L2:
    Description: Production application
    Checks: Security + integration + deployment
  L3:
    Description: Business-critical
    Checks: Performance + security + observability
  L4:
    Description: High-scale
    Checks: Resilience + DR + advanced security
  L5:
    Description: Mission-critical
    Checks: Formal controls + continuous verification

GateMatrix:
  | Gate            | L1 | L2 | L3 | L4 | L5 |
  | --------------- | -- | -- | -- | -- | -- |
  | Lint            | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
  | Unit            | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
  | Integration     | opt | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
  | E2E             | opt | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
  | SAST            | opt | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
  | DAST            | ❌ | opt | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
  | Pentest         | ❌ | risk | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
  | Load            | ❌ | risk | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
  | DDoS resilience | ❌ | ❌ | opt | ✅ | ✅ |
  | DR              | ❌ | opt | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |

QualityProfile:
  ProjectLevel: <L0-L5>
  BusinessCriticality: <LOW|MEDIUM|HIGH|CRITICAL>
  DataSensitivity: <LOW|MEDIUM|HIGH>
  InternetExposure: <YES|NO>
  Scale: <DAU/MAU/RPS>

LevelRules:
  [LV1]  Gate selection is based on project level and context.
  [LV2]  Default matrix may be overridden by project-specific policy.
  [LV3]  Higher levels include all lower level gates.

State: +
  